    "agent_last_message": "I've written the tool at `output/main.py`. It uses only the standard library and runs as `python main.py --input <file> --output <file>`.\n\nI ran it on a few small files and the results matched the spec:\n- **Normal text:** a mixed-case sample file gave the right counts, and `hello` and `hello,` were counted as different words.\n- **Empty file:** all counts were 0 and `top_words` was empty.\n- **Whitespace-only file:** `\\n\\n\\n` gave 3 lines and 0 words.\n- **Exit code 1:** it exited 1 for a missing input file, a missing `--output`, an unknown flag, and a file with invalid UTF-8.\n\nI did not test large files, an unwritable output path, or exit code 2.\n\n- **Characters:** the count is bytes, as the spec says.\n- **Word splitting:** words are split only on the six whitespace characters the spec lists. Unicode spaces such as a non-breaking space stay part of the word.\n- **Large files:** the file is read in 1 MB chunks, so memory use doesn't grow with file size. It does grow with the number of distinct words.\n- **Invalid UTF-8:** I treated this as \"malformed\" input and exit 1, since the spec doesn't say what to do with it.\n- **Output path:** a failure to write the output file also exits 1.\n- **Other errors:** any other unexpected error, including running out of memory, exits 2.",
